#: ../../../dev/errno.md:112
msgid "Why `libc_errno` Header and Runtime Storage Are Separated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/errno.md:114
msgid ""
"Keeping `libc.src.__support.libc_errno` (header) separate from "
"`libc.src.errno.errno` (runtime object) is necessary for several reasons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/errno.md:117
msgid ""
"**Isolating unit tests from host `errno` in overlay mode**: Public overlay "
"archives (`libllvmlibc.a`) are built with `-DLIBC_COPT_PUBLIC_PACKAGING` and "
"use the host's `<errno.h>` (`LIBC_ERRNO_MODE_SYSTEM_INLINE`). Unit tests are "
"built without `-DLIBC_COPT_PUBLIC_PACKAGING` and use LLVM-libc's internal "
"`thread_errno` (`LIBC_ERRNO_MODE_THREAD_LOCAL`), preventing tested functions "
"from clobbering the host `errno` used by the test harness. Conversely, if "
"internal code or tests mistakenly `#include <errno.h>` and use `errno` "
"directly, reads and writes will hit different thread-local variables in the "
"same thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/errno.md:126
msgid ""
"**Header-only `libc/shared/*` consumption**: External LLVM subprojects (such "
"as `libc++` and `offload`) include headers under `libc/shared/`, which set "
"`LIBC_ERRNO_MODE_SYSTEM_INLINE` and map `libc_errno` to `<errno.h>` without "
"compiling or linking `libc_errno.cpp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/errno.md:130
msgid ""
"**`errno`-free math and archive separation (`libc.a` vs. `libm.a` / "
"`libmvec.a`)**: `FEnvImpl.h` includes `src/__support/libc_errno.h` to define "
"`fputil::set_errno_if_required`, which is guarded by `#ifndef "
"LIBC_MATH_HAS_NO_ERRNO`. Because `Errno` methods are inline, functions that "
"never call `set_errno_if_required` (such as `ceil`, `floor`, `copysign`, "
"vector math, or `LIBC_MATH_NO_ERRNO` builds) emit no reference to "
"`__llvm_libc_errno()`, and `libc.src.errno.errno` stays in `libc.a` rather "
"than being pulled into `libm.a` or `libmvec.a`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/errno.md:138
msgid ""
"**CMake directory ordering**: `libc/src/CMakeLists.txt` adds `src/__support` "
"before `src/errno` because `libc.src.errno.errno` depends on "
"`libc.src.__support.*`. Targets under `libc/src/__support/` therefore cannot "
"depend on `libc.src.errno.errno`."
msgstr ""
